---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site, mailHref } from '../data/site';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Website terms of use"
  path="/terms/"
  updated="29 October 2026"
  description="Terms of use for the Apex Global Consulting Services website, including the general-information disclaimer for articles and website content."
>
  <p>
    These terms govern your use of www.apexglobalconsultants.co.uk. By using the website you accept them. If you do not agree, please do not use the
    website.
  </p>

  <h2>1. About us</h2>
  <p>
    This website is operated by {site.legalName} ("Apex Global", "we", "us"), a private limited company registered in England and Wales, company number
    {site.companyNumber}.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Using our website</h2>
  <p>
    You may use this website for your own information and to contact us. We aim to keep it available and up to date, but we do not guarantee that it will
    be uninterrupted, error-free or free of viruses. We may change, suspend or withdraw any part of the website without notice.
  </p>

  <h2>3. No professional advice</h2>
  <p>
    The content of this website, including articles on tax, accounting and regulatory changes, is general information only. It is not professional advice
    and should not be relied on as such. Tax rules and rates change, and the right answer depends on your circumstances. Please
    <a href="/contact/">speak to us</a> before acting on anything you read here.
  </p>
  <p>
    We only act for clients under a signed engagement letter. Our services are governed by that engagement letter and our terms of business, not by these
    website terms. Contacting us through the website does not create a client relationship.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The website and its content, including text, design, logos and graphics, belong to Apex Global or our licensors and are protected by copyright and
    other intellectual property laws. You may print or download one copy of a page for your own personal, non-commercial use. You may not copy, republish,
    sell or otherwise use any content commercially without our written permission.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You must not use the website:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>for any unlawful or fraudulent purpose</li>
    <li>to send spam or submit false information through our forms</li>
    <li>to introduce viruses or other harmful material, or try to gain unauthorised access to the website or our systems</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We may report any such use to the relevant authorities.</p>

  <h2>6. Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>
    Our website links to other sites, such as HMRC, Companies House and our social media pages. We have no control over those sites and are not responsible
    for their content or how they use your data. You may link to our homepage in a fair and lawful way, but not in a way that suggests an endorsement we
